Enhancement: More flexible formats for backup and rewrite time related options

Restic backup --time allowed in the past only the format "2006-01-02 15:04:05".

`backup --time` and `rewrite --new-time` can now use the following range of date/time
formats:

```
y-m-d
y-m-d HH:MM
y-m-d HH:MM:SS

d.m.y
d.m.y HH:MM
d.m.y HH:MM:SS
```

With additional modifiers for timezone name and timezone offset:

```
y-m-d HH:MM:SS MST
y-m-d HH:MM:SS -0700
y-m-d HH:MM:SS-0700

d.m.y HH:MM:SS MST
d.m.y HH:MM:SS -0700
d.m.y HH:MM:SS-0700
```

